     1	# clinic-agent
     2	
     3	Patient-scheduling agent for the Northbay Clinic Group. Patients reach it by SMS or by the web chat
     4	widget on each clinic's site. It looks up, books, reschedules, and cancels appointments in the EHR,
     5	sends SMS reminders, refunds no-show deposits, and asks the insurance-eligibility agent whether a
     6	visit is covered.
     7	
     8	Each clinic is a tenant. A clinic's patients, appointments, deposits, and EHR credentials are kept
     9	separate from every other clinic's.
    10	
    11	## Components
    12	
    13	| Piece | Where | Notes |
    14	|---|---|---|
    15	| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |
    16	| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |
    17	| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |
    18	| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |
    19	| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |
    20	| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |
    21	| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |
    22	| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |
    23	| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |
    24	| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |
    25	
    26	There is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and
    27	the EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.
    28	
    29	## High-impact actions
    30	
    31	`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for
    32	the approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent
    33	retries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.
    34	
    35	## Stopping the agent
    36	
    37	Operators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a
    38	`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:
    39	
    40	```bash
    41	aws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \
    42	  --item '{"pk":{"S":"global"},"halted":{"BOOL":true},"by":{"S":"<you>"}}'
    43	```
    44	
    45	Running work checks the flag before each model turn and each tool call, and a watcher aborts in-flight
    46	requests within 2 seconds.
    47	
    48	## Identity
    49	
    50	`src/agent/identity.ts` computes the agent-type-id from the image digest, harness version, prompts,
    51	model IDs, and config. Each pod also gets a random agent-instance-id at start. Both are on every
    52	audit record together with the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, and trace context.
    53	
    54	## Build and test
    55	
    56	```bash
    57	npm ci
    58	npm run lint
    59	npm test
    60	npm run build
    61	```
    62	
    63	## Release
    64	
    65	Merges to `main` need two reviews and a code owner review for prompts, config, infra, and manifests.
    66	`deploy.yml` builds, signs, and deploys by digest to the `production` environment, which has required
    67	reviewers. Emergency deploys use the same workflow with `emergency: true` and must name an owner,
    68	a reason, and an end date; the workflow opens a follow-up review issue.
    69	
    70	## Owners
    71	
    72	- Accountable party: Northbay Clinic Group, Patient Access (VP Patient Access)
    73	- Operational owner: agent-platform team, `#agent-platform-oncall`
     1	import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
     2	import { join } from "node:path";
     3	import { parse } from "yaml";
     4	
     5	export const ROOT = process.env.CLINIC_AGENT_ROOT ?? process.cwd();
     6	
     7	export interface Policy {
     8	  version: string;
     9	  highImpactTools: string[];
    10	  approval: { ttlSeconds: number; approverRoles: string[]; table: string };
    11	}
    12	
    13	export interface AllowlistEntry {
    14	  tool: string;
    15	  reason: string;
    16	}
    17	
    18	export interface Budgets {
    19	  run: {
    20	    maxTurns: number;
    21	    maxWallMs: number;
    22	    maxInputTokens: number;
    23	    maxOutputTokens: number;
    24	    maxCostUsd: number;
    25	    maxToolCalls: number;
    26	    maxToolCallsPerMinute: number;
    27	    maxPeerCalls: number;
    28	  };
    29	  quotas: {
    30	    perSubjectDailyUsd: number;
    31	    perTenantDailyUsd: number;
    32	    fleetDailyUsd: number;
    33	    perTenantToolCallsPerMinute: number;
    34	    fleetToolCallsPerMinute: number;
    35	  };
    36	  pricingUsdPerMTok: Record<string, { input: number; output: number; cacheRead: number; cacheWrite: number }>;
    37	  onExceed: "handoff_to_staff";
    38	}
    39	
    40	function loadYaml<T>(rel: string): T {
    41	  return parse(readFileSync(join(ROOT, rel), "utf8")) as T;
    42	}
    43	
    44	export const policy = loadYaml<Policy>("config/policy.yaml");
    45	export const allowlist = loadYaml<{ role: string; tools: AllowlistEntry[] }>("config/tools.allowlist.yaml");
    46	export const budgets = loadYaml<Budgets>("config/budgets.yaml");
    47	export const manifest = JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(ROOT, "release/manifest.json"), "utf8"));
